<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cædwalla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 659–689</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Cædwalla of Wessex</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cædwalla was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a> from about 685 to 688. In a short and violent reign he conquered Sussex, Surrey, Kent and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isle-of-wight">Isle of Wight</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bede">Bede</a> says he set out to wipe out the native population and had the two young brothers of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arwald">Arwald</a> killed after their baptism. He then gave up his throne, travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and was baptised by Pope Sergius I shortly before his death in 689.</p></div>
